WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.934 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Our first guest tonight

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
is Emmy- and
Golden Globe-nominated actress

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:04.137 align:start size:94% position:6%
for her work on NBC's
"This Is Us,"

00:00:04.137 --> 00:00:06.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
which returns
with new shows in January.

00:00:06.639 --> 00:00:10.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
Her new holiday songs,
released as a two-track single

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How Could This Be Christmas?"
are available now.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:15.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back to the sho
our friend Mandy Moore.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:17.317 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hi, Mandy!
How are you?

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.252 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm well.
How are you?

00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:20.553 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-I'm doing wonderfully.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:24.357
This has been a weird time i
between your visits to the show.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:27.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
The last time you were her
was in September 2016.

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:31.498 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you have waited
for the entire Trump presidenc

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:33.033 size:75% position:38% line:92%
until you came back.

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know!
I just completely, like,

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
wanted to boycott the show
I guess,

00:00:37.103 --> 00:00:37.904 line:92%
during the Trump presidency.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:39.939
-You were like, "I don't wan
to have any part of that."

00:00:39.939 --> 00:00:41.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-It's lovely to see you again,

00:00:41.541 --> 00:00:45.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
and congratulations.
You're about to have a baby.

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:48.348 align:start size:94% position:6%
How far along are you?
-I am seven months.

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:49.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, my goodness.
-Yeah. I'm getting --

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:52.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
getting towards the end here
but thank you very much.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And you're having a boy,
which I can tell you

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
from experience
is a wonderful thing.

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.725 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I know when you were here,
you know, we talked about

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:02.996
how you watched YouTube videos
of people going through labo

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:05.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
to have triplets
because of your show.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
Does it make it a little bit
easier knowing that

00:01:08.301 --> 00:01:10.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're just
gonna have the one?

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.772 size:84% position:42%
-Is that not normal,
to watch YouTube videos

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.374 line:92%
of people having triplets?

00:01:14.374 --> 00:01:15.775 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, at least
you had a reason.

00:01:15.775 --> 00:01:19.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
It would be weird if you had
no reason to do it.

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:22.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
I've tried to actually forge

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:25.251
the trauma that I endured
watching those videos,

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:28.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
because some of them
are just downright terrifying.

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:30.423 line:92%
So, yes, I'm very grateful

00:01:30.423 --> 00:01:34.260 size:75% position:38%
that I'm just having
one child at a time.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.895 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You guys are back
to filming again,

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:39.365 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you've decided to sort o
take head-on the times

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:43.336
we're living in, from things
like the George Floyd protests

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:44.370 line:92%
to living under quarantine

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:48.174
Is it surreal to be doing a show
that is also, you know,

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.176 line:92%
art imitating life, I guess?

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:54.814
-I mean, I kind of would expec
nothing less from "This Is Us.

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:58.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, we are a modern show
and so much of our show

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:02.155 size:84% position:42%
sort of takes place in,
you know, modern times.

00:02:02.155 --> 00:02:03.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so it would feel weird
I think,

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:08.027 align:start size:94% position:6%
to leave such pressing issue
unaddressed.

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:10.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's certainly weird
because, yeah.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:13.600
I mean, we're living through
COVID, as everybody else is,

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we're shooting
in the midst of COVID.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:18.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we have all of these, like
crazy COVID protocols,

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:21.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
which I'm sure you do, as well
at your show.

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:26.045
So it's certainly strange to
like, have to initially --

00:02:26.045 --> 00:02:27.447 size:78% position:39%
I think we're sort of
past this point now,

00:02:27.447 --> 00:02:29.082 size:81% position:41%
but, like, as an actor
when you're in a scene

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:30.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're looking
all around you

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:33.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the entire crew
is not only in masks

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:35.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
but also in face shields
and other PPE,

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:40.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
to just sort of let that g
and to kind of be in the momen

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:43.429
was definitely, you know,
a bit strange at first,

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:47.534
but now it feels -- it feels
like, you know, second nature.

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:50.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Also, I know, early on,
obviously, in the first season

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:52.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the show, you had to wear
a fake pregnancy belly.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:55.241
Are you a little upset now
that they have not written

00:02:55.241 --> 00:02:58.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
your real one into the show?
-I know.

00:02:58.111 --> 00:03:01.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's funny because
the trajectory of our show is,

00:03:01.047 --> 00:03:03.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
we sort of jump around in time
all the time.

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:06.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I am constantly --
In fact, the very first episod

00:03:06.753 --> 00:03:11.691
I was in, we sort of, like, took
it back to going to the hospital

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:13.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
to give birth
to the triplets that day.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:17.030 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I was in, like, the full,
heavy, like,

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:20.033 size:84% position:42%
eight-month prosthetic
triplet belly and boobs

00:03:20.033 --> 00:03:23.203
and, like, the whole thing
and I'm like, "Geez Louise

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:25.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
could we not, like,
postpone this for just

00:03:25.638 --> 00:03:29.142
a few more months, and I could
you know, help out a little bi

00:03:29.142 --> 00:03:31.044 line:92%
myself with my own body?"

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:32.912 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, of course, I think,
like, true to form,

00:03:32.912 --> 00:03:36.082
by the time I am, like, waddling
around at nine months pregnant

00:03:36.082 --> 00:03:38.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
we'd probably be shooting
something where I'm supposed

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.486 line:92%
to be like 25 and fresh-face

00:03:40.486 --> 00:03:43.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
and getting married
or something ridiculous.

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:44.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-So, just --

00:03:44.657 --> 00:03:48.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
just what I sort of
come to expect from this job

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:51.598
-So you decided to record
a couple of holiday songs.

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:54.901
How did this come about,
the decision to want to do this?

00:03:54.901 --> 00:03:58.004
-So, I put out a record,
called "Silver Landings,"

00:03:58.004 --> 00:04:01.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
earlier this year, and we were
literally four days away

00:04:01.107 --> 00:04:03.343 size:84% position:42%
from going on the road,
my first time touring

00:04:03.343 --> 00:04:07.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
in 13 years, and COVID hit
and, obviously,

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:09.015 line:92%
the world sort of had to shift

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:12.085 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, I've been home
with my husband, obviously

00:04:12.085 --> 00:04:13.353 line:92%
like most people quarantinin

00:04:13.353 --> 00:04:14.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the last eight
or nine months.

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:17.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a couple months ago,
it just sort of struck me that

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:20.760
in order to expend sort of this,
like, pent-up creative energy,

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.430
it might be fun to not onl
record a cover of, like,

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:27.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
a classic Christmas song,
but then try our hand

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
at writing one,
and I think

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:33.106
"How Could This Be Christmas?"
was the original that we wrote

00:04:33.106 --> 00:04:36.676
and it sort of really reflects
on, like, this very specific

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:39.712
and strange holiday that we're
all going to be living through

00:04:39.712 --> 00:04:44.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
and sort of rooted in the idea
that, really, it's about

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
togetherness and connection,
and that's something

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:49.922 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is gonna look
a little different this year

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:52.558
You know?
-When you decided a cover, like,

00:04:52.558 --> 00:04:55.695
did you have a lot of choices in
front of you or was it obvious

00:04:55.695 --> 00:04:57.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure.
You know, considering that

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.066
we were gonna acknowledge
what this holiday was,

00:05:00.066 --> 00:05:03.069 align:start size:94% position:6%
specifically, in 2020, wit
"How Could This Be Christmas?"

00:05:03.069 --> 00:05:05.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
we thought it would be, like
a perfect bookend

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:08.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
to "The Most Wonderful
Time of the Year,"

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:09.642 size:84% position:42% line:92%
like, by Andy Williams.

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:12.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just, I mean, I felt like it
sort of covered, like,

00:05:12.045 --> 00:05:15.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
the spectrum of emotions
that we're all gonna be feelin

00:05:15.114 --> 00:05:17.216 size:78% position:39%
during the holidays.
-I feel like everyone

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:20.953
will slowly be rotating
back and forth between those two

00:05:20.953 --> 00:05:23.489 align:start size:94% position:6%
of, "This is the Most Wonderfu
Time of the Year"

00:05:23.489 --> 00:05:25.158 align:start size:94% position:6%
and "Oh, my God.
This is a hellscape.

00:05:25.158 --> 00:05:27.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't care how many ornament
are on the tree."

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:30.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mentioned in the tease -
you probably weren't on yet --

00:05:30.797 --> 00:05:32.265 line:92%
but we were in a film together

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:34.767 align:start size:94% position:6%
You remember
the name of the film, right?

00:05:34.767 --> 00:05:36.602
-"American Dreamz," yeah.
-Yeah, well, guess what.

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:39.072 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hugh Grant was on the show
and he had no memory

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:40.673 line:92%
that he ever worked with me.

00:05:40.673 --> 00:05:43.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, that is so deflating
and disappointing.

00:05:43.776 --> 00:05:45.345 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
But I guarantee, by the way,

00:05:45.345 --> 00:05:47.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
he probably has no idea
that he worked with me, either

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No. When I told him
the name of it, he's like,

00:05:49.148 --> 00:05:51.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh! With Mandy Moore.
She was wonderful."

00:05:51.551 --> 00:05:53.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-No, really?

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:55.855 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, but still...
-Yeah, see? Exactly.

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:58.458
I swear, I crossed paths
with him at an award shows

00:05:58.458 --> 00:05:59.492 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and I was like, "Hi,"

00:05:59.492 --> 00:06:02.261 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he looked at me
like I had four heads.

00:06:02.261 --> 00:06:03.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
-So, I'm -- I'm --

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:08.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's a lovely man, but, yo
know, he does a ton of movies.

00:06:08.301 --> 00:06:09.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know.
But I will never forget.

00:06:09.836 --> 00:06:13.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had the best time with you
-We had a great time.

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:15.942
-I came out of that projec
going, like, "Seth Meyers

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:19.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
is probably the funniest perso
I've ever met in my life."

00:06:19.746 --> 00:06:23.649 size:84% position:42%
-Right. You were like,
"Not the best actor..."

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:24.951 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:26.185 line:92%
"Like, I wouldn't be surprised

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:28.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
if this was
one of his last movies."

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:30.690 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:32.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
Mandy, I have great memories
of that,

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:35.094 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it is always
just so lovely to see you.

00:06:35.094 --> 00:06:36.396 line:92%
Thanks so much for being here.

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:37.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you for having me.
Good to see you.

00:06:37.697 --> 00:06:41.033 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Her new holiday music,
"How Could This Be Christmas?"

00:06:41.033 --> 00:06:42.935 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is available now.

